ID: B2-Ch05a-Intro
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch2_deal != 3 && v_b2_ch2_lessathi != 0 || v_b2_ch2_deal != 3 && v_b2_ch2_threatened != 2) {
 

"Stillwater!" Bruce snaps his fingers in front of my face. "Hey. Stillwater. You in there?"

The stone holding cell snaps back into focus. My head is still full of troll regeneration notes and arena layouts, and I have completely lost track of the room. Wilhelm is already back from the sands, leaning against the far wall with his arms crossed, while Bruce glares at me with his hands on his hips. He definitely asked me something, and I definitely did not hear a single syllable.

"Missed that," I say, blinking against the torchlight. "Say it again."

"Wilhelm," Bruce says, jerking his chin toward the assassin. "We can't let him wander the arena after that stunt in the first round. He'll put a blade in someone's back the second we look away. I say we tie him up and leave him on the floor. Safer for everyone."

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 0 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2 || v_b2_ch2_deal == 3) {
 

"Stillwater!" Bruce snaps his fingers in front of my face. "Hey. Stillwater. You in there?"

The stone holding cell snaps back into focus. My head is still full of troll regeneration notes and arena layouts, and I have completely lost track of the room. Wilhelm is already back from the sands, leaning against the far wall with his arms crossed, while Bruce glares at me with his hands on his hips. He definitely asked me something, and I definitely did not hear a single syllable.

"Missed that," I say, blinking against the torchlight. "Say it again."

"Wilhelm," Bruce says, jerking his chin toward the assassin. "You saw that orange-hilted dagger he pulled last round. The man is an assassin, plain and simple. Leaving him loose in the arena is asking for a knife in the spine. I say we tie him up and leave him on the floor. Safer for everyone."

}
choice(""Wilhelm is not a threat. Let him do what he wants. It won't make any difference."", B2-Ch05a-Threat, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Threat, v_checkpoint_rich = 0, v_b2_ch5_wilhelm = 0)
choice(""We don't have any rope. We could just tell him to keep his distance from us."", B2-Ch05a-Rope, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Rope, v_checkpoint_rich = 0, v_b2_ch5_wilhelm = 0)
choice(""Let him fight with us. We'll need all the help we can get against that troll."", B2-Ch05a-Help, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Help, v_checkpoint_rich = 0, v_b2_ch5_wilhelm = 1)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Threat
TEXT:

 "Wilhelm is not a threat. Let him do what he wants. It won't make any difference."

"Easy for you to say," Bruce grunts. "I'd rather not spend the entire match checking over my shoulder for my own teammates. Surviving the first round with him around was headache enough."

"We don't have rope anyway," the mage mutters, keeping his distance from everyone. "And there's no reason to pin him down. If he keeps to the opposite side of the sand, we'll be fine."

Wilhelm offers a thin, flat smile. "If my assistance is unwelcome, you only have to say so once. Rest assured, I will give all of you a very wide berth."

My train of thought derails. The ambient roar of the crowd floods back in, scraping against the stone walls. What was I working through before Bruce started shouting? Something about the troll.

I step up to the iron grate and look out into the sunlit bowl. Out on the blood-soaked sand, Velgos is still strutting in circles, raising his arms to milk cheers from the upper tiers. The sight of him jogs the memory loose.

"Leila," I say, leaning toward her. "Take a look at his armor. Is it different from the first wave?"

Glowing blue letters materialize in the air between us. "It is still anti-magic plating, but he added pauldrons. He is trying to protect his neck so we cannot decapitate him again."

"Tell me if I'm remembering the alloy right," I say. "Doesn't that specific plating fail against normal flame?"

"It offers no protection against mundane fire," Leila writes, the blue script hanging sharp and clear. "Only magical fire."

"That's what I thought." I turn toward the corridor door.

My hand rests on the iron latch, and I glance back at Leila.

"Do me a favor," I tell her in a low voice. "Grab one of the wall torches from the hallway before the gate goes up. Keep it behind your back when you step onto the sand so Velgos doesn't clock it. Once we're both out there, wait for my signal, then throw it straight at him. Understood?"

"Understood. But where are you going?" she writes. "What are you doing?"

"You'll see in a minute," I say, and slip out into the corridor.

The hall is quiet. No arena guards in my immediate line of sight. I head straight for the second division's prep area—Hadrik's room should be only a few doors down.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Ogres-heard, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Ogres-heard, v_b2_ch5_heard_guards = 1) if (v_hearing >= 2)
