ID: B2-Ch05a-Rope
TEXT:

 "We don't have any rope. We could just tell him to keep his distance from us."

"That works," the mage says quickly. "As long as he stays far away on the other side of the sand, we shouldn't have problems."

Wilhelm gives a slight bow. "If my assistance is unwelcome, you only have to say so once. Rest assured, I will give all of you a very wide berth."

My train of thought derails. The ambient roar of the crowd floods back in, scraping against the stone walls. What was I working through before Bruce started shouting? Something about the troll.

