ID: B2-Ch05a-Decoy
TEXT:

set(v_b2_ch5_first_cut,1) if (v_agility >= 3 || v_reflexes >= 3)
set(v_b2_ch5_first_cut,0) if (v_b2_ch5_heard_guards == 0 && v_is_dead == 0 || v_agility < 3 && v_reflexes < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility >= 3 || v_reflexes >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 3 && v_reflexes < 3)
#if(v_agility >= 3) {
 

Leila has the better angle and the faster hands. All I need to do is draw his attention away from her flank.

I charge straight at Velgos, dagger raised high in an exaggerated chest stab. 

I close just far enough to force him into a committed guard, then plant my boot and spring backward at an angle, dragging his focus away and turning his unarmored shoulder squarely toward Leila.

Leila reads the setup instantly. As Velgos tracks my retreat, she closes the distance in a blur, her enchanted dagger whistling through the exposed neck from the shattered pauldron side. The head shears free in one clean stroke. She catches it by the coarse hair, slams it into the dirt, and brings her heavy wooden sandal down with crushing force, pulverizing the skull into the sand.

}
#if(v_reflexes >= 3 && v_agility < 3) {
 

Leila has the better angle and the faster hands. All I need to do is draw his attention away from her flank.

I charge straight at Velgos, dagger raised high in an exaggerated chest stab.

I push in close to provoke a strike, then try to backpedal, but my foot catches on a rut in the sand. Velgos slashes with his right scimitar. My instincts kick in; I twist hard beneath the incoming steel, rolling clear and positioning myself so the troll has to turn his back to Leila to track me.

Leila reads the setup instantly. As Velgos tracks my retreat, she closes the distance in a blur, her enchanted dagger whistling through the exposed neck from the shattered pauldron side. The head shears free in one clean stroke. She catches it by the coarse hair, slams it into the dirt, and brings her heavy wooden sandal down with crushing force, pulverizing the skull into the sand.

}
#if(v_agility < 3 && v_reflexes < 3) {
 

Leila has the better angle and the faster hands. All I need to do is draw his attention away from her flank.

I charge straight at Velgos, dagger raised high in an exaggerated chest stab.

I close in to draw his attack, but my retreat is half a step too slow. The troll reads my footing and whips his left scimitar across before I can pull clear. The heavy blade cuts through my neck in an instant, and darkness takes me before I hit the ground.

}
#if(v_agility >= 3 || v_reflexes >= 3) {
 The headless bulk of the troll leaps back, but the crushed mess on the sand stays inert. Instead, new tissue bubbles rapidly from the neck stump. Within five seconds a fresh head forms, its features twitching with raw agony as the skin knits shut.

"I will carve you into pieces," Velgos rasps, coughing black bile. "Slowly. While your friends watch."

"Yeah, yeah," I say. "Heard it all before."

"Behind you! Heads up!" Bruce roars from the rear.

A pair of massive, slate-gray ogres thunder through the gate behind Velgos, brandishing iron-banded tree trunks for clubs. Leila and I spring backward, falling in with the rest of our division as the line forms up on the sand.

"I knew it," the fire mage whimpers, gripping his staff with white knuckles. "I knew they wouldn't let us fight just the troll. They had to throw ogres into the pen!"

"Quit whining," Bruce barks, cracking his knuckles. "Ogres are big, dumb, and slow. I can snap both their necks myself."

}
