ID: B2-Ch05a-Tactical
TEXT:

 We should not trade blows out here isolated. We took off one of his pauldrons; that gives us the opening we need for later.

I flash a hand signal to Leila, and we both break off, falling back across the sand to link up with the rest of our division. Velgos is still shaking off the burns, tusks steaming in the arena air, and holds his ground rather than pursuing. Behind him, two massive, slate-gray ogres emerge through the gate, dragging iron-banded tree trunks across the dirt.

"I knew it," the fire mage whimpers, his hands shaking around his staff. "I knew they wouldn't let us fight just the troll. They had to throw ogres into the pen!"

"Quit whining," Bruce barks, rolling his shoulders. "Ogres are big, dumb, and slow. I can snap both their necks myself."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Not-Heard, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Not-Heard) if (v_b2_ch5_heard_guards == 0 && v_is_dead == 0)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Heard, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Heard) if (v_b2_ch5_heard_guards == 1 && v_is_dead == 0)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Not-Heard
TEXT:

set(v_b2_ch5_negotiate,0)
 "Keep your guard up," I tell Bruce. "I've tangled with mountain ogres across the western continent, and these two are heavier and faster than standard stock."

"Bah!" Bruce spits into the sand. "Mass doesn't scare me. Big or small, everything bleeds when you put steel in it."

The beasts don't grant us time to argue. They charge shoulder to shoulder, guttural roars tearing from their throats as they swing their iron-ringed trunks in sweeping arcs.

"I've got the brutes!" Bruce roars, ducking under an incoming timber. "Get to the troll! Move!"

Leila is already breaking toward the center to engage Velgos. I circle around her flank, fixing my eyes on the troll's guard to find an opening.

