ID: B2-Ch05a-Heard
TEXT:

set(v_b2_ch5_negotiate,0) if (v_ancient_languages == 0)
set(v_b2_ch5_negotiate,1) if (v_ancient_languages >= 1)
#if(v_ancient_languages == 0) {
 

"Actually, let me take these two," I tell Bruce. "I might be able to turn them if I get a word in."

"Sounds like suicide to me," Bruce grunts, "but have at it. You take the meat, I'll take the troll."

The ogres charge before another word can be exchanged, boots shaking the dirt as their massive clubs whistle through the air.

The rest of the division fans out toward the center, leaving me alone in the path of the charge.

"Hey!" I shout, waving an arm. "Hold on! We need to talk!"

Neither brute slows down. An iron-banded club crashes into the sand where I stood a fraction of a second earlier. Their swings carry terrifying weight, but out in the open sand, sidestepping the telegraphed recovery arcs is straightforward work.

"It's about your clan! The captives!" I yell.

Nothing. Not a flicker in their dull, bloodshot eyes.

Common isn't registering. Without a single word of the ogre tongue in my memory, trying to negotiate is just burning oxygen.

}
#if(v_ancient_languages >= 1) {
 

"Actually, let me take these two," I tell Bruce. "I might be able to turn them if I get a word in."

"Sounds like suicide to me," Bruce grunts, "but have at it. You take the meat, I'll take the troll."

The ogres charge before another word can be exchanged, boots shaking the dirt as their massive clubs whistle through the air.

The rest of the division fans out toward the center, leaving me alone in the path of the charge.

"Hey!" I shout, waving an arm. "Hold on! We need to talk!"

Neither brute slows down. An iron-banded club crashes into the sand where I stood a fraction of a second earlier. Their swings carry terrifying weight, but out in the open sand, sidestepping the telegraphed recovery arcs is straightforward work.

"It's about your clan! The captives!" I yell in Common.

Still nothing.

"I know where the troll is holding your kin," I bark in the guttural cadence of the ogre tongue.

Both monsters freeze mid-swing, the heavy clubs dipping in the sand as their wide, yellow eyes fix on me in disbelief.

}
choice("Kill the ogres", B2-Ch05a-Kill-ogres, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Kill-ogres, v_b2_ch5_negotiate = 2) if (v_ancient_languages == 0)
choice("Ask for help in dealing with the ogres", B2-Ch05a-Dealing, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Dealing) if (v_ancient_languages == 0)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Negotiation, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Negotiation) if (v_ancient_languages >= 1)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Negotiation
TEXT:

 "How does a little human know of our blood?" the first ogre growls, words rumbling deep in his chest.

"Do not listen, brother," the second warns, raising his club a fraction. "A trick of the arena."

"Is it?" I say, keeping my tone level in their dialect. "What if I told you one of the prisoners is your tribe's shaman? Robes, chalk ash across her brow."

"He knows of the shaman," the first rumbles, jaw hanging open. "He speaks truth."

"Truth or lies, it changes nothing," the second says, his grip tightening. "The troll slits their throats the moment we defy him."

"Not if his own throat is cut first," I say.

"Madness!" the second snarls. "Velgos cannot die. He rises from every wound. We cannot kill him."

"So you die in the sand as his dogs?" I counter.

"Brother," the first ogre rumbles, stepping between us. "We have bled under his whip long enough. We will never see a cleaner chance to avenge our dead and break the cage."

The second ogre glares at his partner, the heavy wood of his club trembling against the sand as he weighs the risk.

"What do you demand of us, human?"

"Put your weight on the troll," I tell him. "The moment he drops, I give you the holding cell. You break your kin out and clear the city gates before the garrison mobilizes."

"Break your word," the second ogre growls, stepping close enough that I smell rancid fat and sour sweat, "and I crush your skull between my hands."

"I intend to keep it," I say.

They trade one short nod, haul their clubs onto their shoulders, and turn toward Velgos.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Prepare, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Prepare)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Dealing
TEXT:

 "Hey! Team!" I shout across the sand, dodging another massive swing. "Change of plans! I could use a hand over here!"

"Curse it all!" Bruce roars in disgust, breaking away from the center. "Waste of breath! We don't need two men to handle two clumsy brutes. Swap with me. Get on the troll!"

"You think you can just walk away from—" Velgos bellows, but Leila's enchanted blade slashes across his collarbone, forcing him to snap his guard up and swallow the insult.

Bruce slides in with his fists raised to intercept the clubs, and I sprint toward the center, locking my attention on the troll's posture.

choice("Observe the battle between Leila and Velgos, in order to find his weaknesses", B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Wilhelm, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Wilhelm, v_b2_ch5_strategy = 1) if (v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 1 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 0 && v_b2_ch5_wilhelm == 1)
