choice("Cut the troll's head off, while he's busy fighting Leila", B2-Ch05a-Easily-Without-Real, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Easily-Without-Real, v_b2_ch5_strategy = 3) if (v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 0 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 0 && v_b2_ch5_wilhelm == 0)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Kill-ogres
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility >= 2 || v_strength >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 2 && v_strength < 3)
#if(v_agility >= 2) {
 

No time to waste dancing around on the flank. I need to put these two down immediately and get back to Leila.

The span of their iron-banded clubs covers a massive kill zone; closing in without enough speed to clear their return arcs is suicide. I have to either run rings around them or overpower them on the clash.

I charge the right-hand ogre, drawing his windup, then accelerate hard to the left just as the heavy timber smashes into the sand. I slip behind his shoulder and drive my enchanted dagger into his kidney three times in rapid succession. His partner swings to assist, but checks the blow to avoid crushing his companion. The hesitation slows an already sluggish swing; I duck beneath the timber, close the gap in one burst, and bury my blade to the hilt between his ribs. As the second brute collapses, I step over to the first, who is clutching his back in the dirt, and draw the dagger across his throat.

}
#if(v_strength >= 3 && v_agility < 2) {
 

No time to waste dancing around on the flank. I need to put these two down immediately and get back to Leila.

The span of their iron-banded clubs covers a massive kill zone; closing in without enough speed to clear their return arcs is suicide. I have to either run rings around them or overpower them on the clash.

I am not fast enough to dance through their reach, but my stat booster is packed with raw muscle. I plant my boots and wait for the nearest brute to commit. As his massive timber descends, I lock both hands onto the hilt of my dagger and meet the blow overhead.

Wood cracks against enchanted steel. The shock travels down my arms, but my footing holds. I release the dagger with my right hand, seize the iron banding of the club with both fists, and wrench the weapon straight out of the ogre's grip. 

Before he can register his empty hands, I bring the heavy timber down on his crown with all the power in my back. His skull shatters like dry clay. I pivot on my heel and swing the stolen log in a flat arc at the second ogre. With equal reach, his sluggish windup is a fatal liability. My swing connects across his jaw before his own stroke clears his shoulder, sending him crashing onto his side in the dirt. 

I drop the splintered club and retrieve my knife from the sand. A heavy log works against blunt brutes, but Velgos's enchanted scimitars would shear through timber in one stroke.

}
#if(v_agility < 2 && v_strength < 3) {
 

No time to waste dancing around on the flank. I need to put these two down immediately and get back to Leila.

The span of their iron-banded clubs covers a massive kill zone; closing in without enough speed to clear their return arcs is suicide. I have to either run rings around them or overpower them on the clash.

Then again, ogres are simple and slow. Wit and timing should be enough to navigate the arc.

I charge the nearest brute, tracking his shoulder muscles to predict the downswing. As he lifts the timber, I step laterally to clear the zone. The timing is off. The sheer radius of the iron banding clips my temple mid-step, crushing bone and driving me face-first into the dirt. Darkness claims everything before the second blow falls.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Prepare, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Prepare) if (v_agility >= 2 || v_strength >= 3)
