ID: B2-Ch05a-Prepare
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 0 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 2) {
 Out in the center, Leila and Bruce work the troll in tandem. A clean feint from Bruce opens the line, and Leila's enchanted blade severs Velgos's head cleanly from his shoulders. She drops her wooden sandal onto the severed skull, crushing it into the grit.

The pulp on the ground stays dead. From the neck stump, flesh bubbles furiously, knitting a replacement head in five agonizing seconds. Velgos clutches his throat, his face twisted in torment.

I turn my full attention back toward him, running through angles of attack.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 1 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 2) {
 Out in the center, Leila and Bruce work the troll in tandem, coordinating a second decapitation. Leila's blade shears through the neck, and she crushes the fallen head beneath her wooden sandal.

From the neck stump, the flesh reconstructs much more slowly. The new jaw is lopsided, the skin mottled and incomplete, and Velgos stumbles with both hands clawing at his throat.

I turn my full attention back toward him, running through angles of attack.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 0 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 1) {
 Across the sand, Leila and Bruce execute a clean flank against the troll. Leila's enchanted blade severs Velgos's neck in a single sweep, and she crushes the severed head beneath her wooden sandal.

The pulp on the ground stays dead. From the neck stump, flesh bubbles furiously, knitting a replacement head in five agonizing seconds. Velgos clutches his throat, his face twisted in torment.

I turn my full attention back toward him, running through angles of attack.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 1 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 1) {
 Across the sand, Leila and Bruce execute a clean flank, taking Velgos's head for a second time. Leila's blade shears through the neck, and she crushes the fallen head beneath her wooden sandal.

From the neck stump, the flesh reconstructs much more slowly. The new jaw is lopsided, the skin mottled and incomplete, and Velgos stumbles with both hands clawing at his throat.

I turn my full attention back toward him, running through angles of attack.

}
choice("Observe the battle between Leila and Velgos, in order to find his weaknesses", B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Ogres, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Ogres, v_b2_ch5_strategy = 1)
choice("Lie to the mage, in order to convince him to act as a decoy", B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Ogres, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Ogres, v_b2_ch5_strategy = 2)
choice("Cut the troll's head off, while he's busy fighting Leila", B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Ogres, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Ogres, v_b2_ch5_strategy = 3)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Ogres
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 0 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 2) {
 Velgos catches sight of me across the sand, yellow eyes flaring with fresh fury. Leila exploits the momentary lapse, closing the distance in a low skid to shear his head from his shoulders once again. Her sandal crushes the fallen skull into the sand.

From the neck stump, gray tissue bubbles and stretches into a new head, but the reconstruction lags noticeably. The skin knits unevenly, leaving raw patches of exposed muscle and a crooked jawline.

As the troll stumbles to his feet, Leila and Bruce close in from both flanks, driving him backward with relentless pressure.

"Gods above!" the fire mage cries, waving his hands in exasperation. "Stop cutting off his head! It isn't working!"

"On the contrary!" I call back. "Taking the head is the only thing that works! You saw how long he took to regrow it the second time. Even troll biology has limits. The body burns reserves every time it rebuilds complex tissue. One or two more decapitations and his regeneration will collapse!"

Across the sand, Velgos is losing ground. Bruce draws his high guard while Leila threatens the unarmored shoulder; the moment the troll commits to a swing at Bruce, Leila's blade flashes toward his neck.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 1 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 2) {
 "Gods above!" the fire mage cries, waving his hands in exasperation. "Stop cutting off his head! It isn't working!"

"On the contrary!" I call back. "Taking the head is the only thing that works! You saw how long he took to regrow it the second time. Even troll biology has limits. The body burns reserves every time it rebuilds complex tissue. One or two more decapitations and his regeneration will collapse!"

Across the sand, Velgos locks eyes with me, snarling as his scimitars weave a desperate defensive pattern.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 0 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 1) {
 The two ogres charge the center, timber clubs swinging in wide, bone-cracking sweeps. Velgos's jaw drops in fury at the sight of his former lackeys turning on him. Leila capitalizes on the distraction, sliding under his guard to take his head with one clean stroke. She stomps the skull flat beneath her wooden sandal.

From the neck stump, gray tissue bubbles and stretches into a new head, but the reconstruction drags. The features knit crooked and incomplete, skin missing along the jaw.

As soon as the head forms, Leila, Bruce, and the two ogres surround the troll, pressing him from four sides at once.

"Gods above!" the fire mage cries, waving his hands in exasperation. "Stop cutting off his head! It isn't working!"

"On the contrary!" I call back. "Taking the head is the only thing that works! You saw how long he took to regrow it the second time. Even troll biology has limits. The body burns reserves every time it rebuilds complex tissue. One or two more decapitations and his regeneration will collapse!"

Velgos is completely overwhelmed. He has never fought four heavy melee combatants at once, and his parries are ragged and late.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 1 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 1) {
 "Gods above!" the fire mage cries, waving his hands in exasperation. "Stop cutting off his head! It isn't working!"

"On the contrary!" I call back. "Taking the head is the only thing that works! You saw how long he took to regrow it the second time. Even troll biology has limits. The body burns reserves every time it rebuilds complex tissue. One or two more decapitations and his regeneration will collapse!"

The two ogres slam into the center, iron-banded logs driving Velgos backward as he snarls in disbelief at their betrayal.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Climactic-Ogres, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Climactic-Ogres)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Climactic-Ogres
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 0 && v_b2_ch5_strategy == 1) {
 I hold my position, watching the troll's footwork for a fresh opening. Before I can find one, Leila slips inside his wide scimitar guard and takes his head off at the neck.

Her sandal pulverizes the skull in the sand. From the bloody neck, tissue surges upward to rebuild, but the magic fails.

What emerges is a grotesque mass of malformed flesh. Half the skin is missing, the jaw hangs unhinged, and the eyes bulge blindly from distorted sockets. Worse for Velgos, the windpipe never forms.

The troll wheezes violently, his chest heaving as he claws at the empty air for oxygen. His yellow eyes lock onto Leila and me with pure venom. He opens his mouth to speak, but only wet, rattling clicks escape his throat. He takes two dragging steps toward us, arm outstretched, then drops heavily to his knees. His broad hands claw frantically at his own neck, tearing bloody ruts through the flesh in a desperate bid to open an airway.

His chest shudders once. His hands go limp, and the massive body crashes face-first into the sand.

"Well," I say, lowering my blade. "That was anti-climactic."

}
