ID: B2-Ch05a-Contrary-Without
TEXT:

 Leila catches Velgos leaning heavy on his back foot and shears his head free in a single, fluid stroke. She drives her wooden sandal into the fallen head, grinding it into the dirt. The pulp stays inert, but new flesh knits upward from the neck stump, lagging behind the previous regeneration. The jaw is asymmetrical, the skin mottled and raw.

The moment his eyes open, Leila is back on him, keeping his scimitars locked in front.

"Gods above!" the fire mage cries, waving his hands in exasperation. "Stop cutting off his head! It isn't working!"

"On the contrary!" I call back. "Taking the head is the only thing that works! You saw how long he took to regrow it the second time. Even troll biology has limits. The body burns reserves every time it rebuilds complex tissue. One or two more decapitations and his regeneration will collapse!"

Across the sand, Leila and Velgos circle each other in a tight, lethal stalemate. Neither has a clean opening; every strike is parried or dodged by a hair's breadth.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Observe, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Observe) if (v_b2_ch5_strategy == 1)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Effortlessly, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Effortlessly) if (v_b2_ch5_strategy == 3)
