ID: B2-Ch05a-Observe
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_perception >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_perception < 3)
#if(v_perception >= 3) {
 

I hold my ground, tracking the troll's weight distribution through every clash.

Whenever Leila's blade work threatens to pin his guard, Velgos pushes off his back leg to create separation. But there is a specific trigger: he only leaps clear when the pressure lands on the left side where the pauldron was stripped. On his armored flank, he plants his boots and absorbs the blow.

I wait for Leila to drive hard against his vulnerable shoulder. The moment Velgos shifts his weight to spring backward, I sprint behind him, matching his trajectory. As his boots leave the sand, I bury Daren's enchanted dagger deep into the small of his back.

The impact knocks him off-axis in mid-air. He stumbles as he lands, guard wide open, and Leila's blade sweeps in like silver lightning to sever his neck cleanly from his shoulders.

}
#if(v_perception < 3) {
 

I hold my ground, tracking the troll's movements across the sand.

Whenever Leila's attacks press his guard, Velgos leaps backward to reset his stance. It looks like a predictable pattern. All I have to do is position myself behind him and plant a blade in his spine as he lands.

Leila steps in with a flurry of strikes. I sprint forward, anticipating the leap.

The retreat is a trap. Velgos doesn't spring to recover balance; he shifts weight deliberately, baiting my approach. As I commit to the thrust, his right scimitar whips around in a flat, blinding backhand. The edge cleaves through my neck before my blade even touches his armor. Darkness swallows the arena before my corpse hits the sand.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Troll-final, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Troll-final) if (v_perception >= 3)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_perception < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_perception < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_perception < 3)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Effortlessly
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_strength >= 2)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_strength < 2)
#if(v_strength >= 2) {
 

"Pleasure chatting with you," I tell the fire mage, "but I've got a troll to butcher, so if you'll excuse me, I'll be off."

I leave him trembling in the dust and sprint toward the center. Velgos cannot spare a fraction of a second to look away from Leila's flashing daggers. I slip behind his unarmored left shoulder without resistance and drive my enchanted dagger through his neck in one clean, violent sweep.

The head tumbles to the sand. I step forward and bring my boot down hard, grinding the skull into bone meal before the troll's body can react.

}
#if(v_strength < 2) {
 

"Pleasure chatting with you," I tell the fire mage, "but I've got a troll to butcher, so if you'll excuse me, I'll be off."

I leave him trembling in the dust and sprint toward the center. Velgos is locked onto Leila's daggers, giving me a clean path to his unarmored shoulder. I drive my dagger across his throat.

The blow lacks the raw power to sever the spine. The blade jams halfway through meat and bone. Before I can wrench it loose and spring clear, Velgos's left hand clamps around my wrist like an iron vise. His right scimitar drives straight through my ribcage. As agony paralyzes my limbs, he wrenches the blade free and takes my head with a single backhand sweep.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Troll-final, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Troll-final) if (v_strength >= 2)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_strength < 2)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_strength < 2)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_strength < 2)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Mage
TEXT:

 "Listen," I tell the fire mage in a hurried whisper. "I have a plan to bring him down, but I need you on the flank."

"What kind of plan?" the mage asks, clutching his staff.

"Velgos is struggling to match Leila's speed," I say, keeping my voice steady and urgent. "He keeps shifting his footing because he can't parry her fast enough. If the two of us close in from behind, pinching him from left and right, he has nowhere to step. Leila takes his head without a fight. It's completely risk-free—he loses his head before he can even target us."

"I... I suppose I can do that," the mage mutters, swallowing hard. "If there's no danger..."

"None at all. Let's move!"

I sprint for the center, and the mage scrambles to keep pace. Presenting a zero-risk opening is the only way to get him moving. He has been frozen in terror since the horn blew, but he doesn't want to look like a coward in front of the crowd.

I conveniently left out one critical detail. Even with his head severed, a troll's dying frame carries enough violent reflex to swing a blade during the first second after decapitation. That is why I have no intention of stabbing Velgos myself. The mage can take the glory—and the return stroke.

We reach the troll's blind side while Leila keeps his scimitars occupied. I flash a nod to the mage, and we both charge his exposed back.

The moment we close the distance, I plant my boots and leap backward out of reach. The mage thrusts his dagger into the troll's spine alone. He stares at me in sudden, horrified betrayal, but Velgos's left scimitar is already whipping around toward his ribs.

Leila capitalizes on the opening. Her enchanted blade shears through the troll's neck in a heartbeat. The lethal decapitation arrests Velgos's swing mid-arc, the whistling steel grazing the mage's robes as he yanks his dagger free and scrambles backward across the sand. Leila stomps the fallen head into dust beneath her wooden sandal.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Troll-final, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Troll-final)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Troll-final
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 1 || v_b2_ch5_strategy == 2 || v_b2_ch5_wilhelm != 0) {
 Her sandal pulverizes the skull in the sand. From the bloody neck, tissue surges upward to rebuild, but the magic fails.

What emerges is a grotesque mass of malformed flesh. Half the skin is missing, the jaw hangs unhinged, and the eyes bulge blindly from distorted sockets. Worse for Velgos, the windpipe never forms.

The troll wheezes violently, his chest heaving as he claws at the empty air for oxygen. His yellow eyes lock onto Leila and me with pure venom. He opens his mouth to speak, but only wet, rattling clicks escape his throat. He takes two dragging steps toward us, arm outstretched, then drops heavily to his knees. His broad hands claw frantically at his own neck, tearing bloody ruts through the flesh in a desperate bid to open an airway.

His chest shudders once. His hands go limp, and the massive body crashes face-first into the sand.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 0 && v_b2_ch5_wilhelm == 0 && v_b2_ch5_strategy != 2) {
 Velgos regrows his head from the neck stump, but the reconstruction lags badly. The skin is mottled, the jaw distorted and slack. We give him no quarter, pressing the attack from both flanks before his vision clears. Leila darts inside his parry, shears through his neck for a third time, and crushes the fallen skull beneath her wooden sandal.

From the bloody neck, tissue surges upward to rebuild, but the magic fails.

What emerges is a grotesque mass of malformed flesh. Half the skin is missing, the jaw hangs unhinged, and the eyes bulge blindly from distorted sockets. Worse for Velgos, the windpipe never forms.

The troll wheezes violently, his chest heaving as he claws at the empty air for oxygen. His yellow eyes lock onto Leila and me with pure venom. He opens his mouth to speak, but only wet, rattling clicks escape his throat. He takes two dragging steps toward us, arm outstretched, then drops heavily to his knees. His broad hands claw frantically at his own neck, tearing bloody ruts through the flesh in a desperate bid to open an airway.

His chest shudders once. His hands go limp, and the massive body crashes face-first into the sand.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Troll-dead, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Troll-dead)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Easily-Without
TEXT:

 Leila catches Velgos leaning heavy on his back foot and shears his head free in a single, fluid stroke. She drives her wooden sandal into the fallen head, grinding it into the dirt. The pulp stays inert, but new flesh knits from the neck stump, taking five agonizing seconds to reconstruct. Velgos clutches his throat, grimacing in torment.

The moment his vision clears, Leila is back on him, keeping his scimitars locked in front.

"Why is she still cutting the head?" the fire mage cries. "Can't she see it isn't working?"

"I wouldn't say that," I tell him. "Look at the pain in his eyes. Rebuilding a head burns enormous reserves. He can't keep that trick up forever. We force him to regrow it until his body gives out!"

Across the sand, Wilhelm repeatedly slips into the troll's blind spots, harrying his flanks. But during the next exchange, a glancing blow from Velgos's scimitar catches Wilhelm across the shoulder, forcing the assassin to retreat toward the perimeter to bind the wound.

Leila capitalizes on the opening, shearing the troll's neck again. The head regenerates even slower, the jaw lopsided and incomplete. Leila gives him no room to recover, driving her daggers forward to press the advantage.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Observe, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Observe) if (v_b2_ch5_strategy == 1)
