"What kind of plan?" the mage asks, clutching his staff.

"Velgos is struggling to match Leila's speed," I say, keeping my voice steady and urgent. "He keeps shifting his footing because he can't parry her fast enough. If the two of us close in from behind, pinching him from left and right, he has nowhere to step. Leila takes his head without a fight. It's completely risk-free—he loses his head before he can even target us."

"I... I suppose I can do that," the mage mutters, swallowing hard. "If there's no danger..."

"None at all. Let's move!"

I sprint for the center, and the mage scrambles to keep pace. Presenting a zero-risk opening is the only way to get him moving. He has been frozen in terror since the horn blew, but he doesn't want to look like a coward in front of the crowd.

I conveniently left out one critical detail. Even with his head severed, a troll's dying frame carries enough violent reflex to swing a blade during the first second after decapitation. That is why I have no intention of stabbing Velgos myself. The mage can take the glory—and the return stroke.

We reach the troll's blind side while Leila keeps his scimitars occupied. I flash a nod to the mage, and we both charge his exposed back.

The moment we close the distance, I plant my boots and leap backward out of reach. The mage thrusts his dagger into the troll's spine alone. He stares at me in sudden, horrified betrayal, but Velgos's left scimitar is already whipping around toward his ribs.

Leila capitalizes on the opening. Her enchanted blade shears through the troll's neck in a heartbeat. The lethal decapitation does not halt Velgos's swing in time; the heavy scimitar whistles inches from the mage's throat.

At the very last instant, the mage springs backward in an unnatural burst of speed, clearing the steel arc by mere inches.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Mage-Helped, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Mage-Helped) if (v_b2_ch2_cell != 1)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Mage-Cell1, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Mage-Cell1) if (v_b2_ch2_cell == 1)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Mage-Helped
TEXT:

 That kind of acceleration doesn't come from human muscle. He must have triggered his scrap stat booster under the robes.

Across the sand, Leila crushes the fallen skull beneath her wooden sandal. From the bloody neck stump, the tissue reconstructs at a crawl, the new jaw lopsided and distorted.

"You set me up!" the mage snarls, stumbling backward with dagger drawn. "You used me as bait!"

"Is this really the time to argue?" I call out. "Your device has a timer, doesn't it? Put it to work while you have the stats!"

The mage gnashes his teeth, swallows the curse, and turns back toward the center with his blade raised.

"Curse you!" he spits, charging back into the fray.

Flanked on both sides, Velgos cannot protect his blind spot. Leila slips past his guard, severs his neck for a third time, and grinds the fallen head into dust.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Troll-final, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Troll-final)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Mage-Cell1
TEXT:

 That speed rivaled Leila's with her device active. The mage is definitely running an enhancer under those robes.

Across the sand, Leila crushes the fallen skull beneath her wooden sandal. From the bloody neck stump, the tissue reconstructs at a crawl, the new jaw lopsided and distorted.

Before the melee can resume, a deafening siren shrieks through the amphitheater. The mage's right pocket flares with blinding crimson light. He clamps a hand over his hip in sheer panic, but the beacon burns straight through the fabric.

"Ladies and gentlemen, pray pardon the interruption," the announcer's amplified voice echoes over the crowd. "Our magical resonance sensors have detected an unauthorized casting device. Will the combatant glowing red please remain stationary? Colosseum enforcers are en route to secure you."

Half a dozen armored guards vault into the pit, longswords drawn.

"All other gladiators, ignore the intervention and continue your bouts in an orderly fashion!"

Leila and Velgos freeze, tracking the guards while keeping their weapons braced against each other. Bruce and the ogres pay the commotion no mind, heavy clubs still smashing into the sand.

"No..." the mage whispers, backing toward the wall.

The guards encircle him in a tight ring. The lead enforcer reaches out an armored gauntlet to seize his shoulder.

"You're coming with us. Move."

"Don't touch me!" The mage wrenches his arm back.

"Don't make this difficult," the guard sneers, stepping forward with his sword raised. "Your life is forfeit either way. Walk quietly or we drag your corpse."

"I said get away!"

Flames erupt from the mage's palms in a roaring cone, engulfing the lead guard instantly. The man collapses into a shrieking pyre of charred flesh and blackened mail.

The other guards lunge forward to pin him, but the mage thrusts both arms wide. A concussive shockwave of fire detonates outward, vaporizing the entire patrol in a blinding flash of ash and cinders.

"Guards!" the announcer screams into his horn, his voice cracking with terror. "All posts to the arena floor! We have a rogue fire elementalist on a rampage! I repeat! Rogue elementalist on the loose!"

The mage stands amidst the burning remains, panting heavily, eyes wide and unhinged. Then his gaze locks onto me across the sand. The shock in his face hardens into homicidal rage.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05a-Mage-Rampage, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05a-Mage-Rampage)


ID: B2-Ch05a-Mage-Rampage
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch5_tribal,1) if (v_agility >= 2)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility >= 2)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 2)
achievement("Tribal dancer",v_ac_b2_ch5_tribal)
#if(v_agility >= 2) {
 

"You!" the mage howls, raising burning hands. "You set me up! I'll burn your flesh to the bone!"

"Hold on, let's talk about—"

A roaring lance of orange flame cuts me off, streaking across the sand at chest height.

I throw myself laterally. The heat scorches my cheek as I roll, but the moment my boots find purchase, the sand beneath my feet turns molten red. A geyser of flame detonates from below. I vault clear just before the column erupts, but the mage snaps his fingers, chaining pillar after pillar directly beneath my landing zones.

"Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!" I scramble in continuous bounds, leaping from one footprint to the next like a man dancing on hot coals.

Attacking him is suicide while he controls the ground. Is he legally an enemy now that he broke the arena ban? Will the archers shoot me if I put a dagger in his throat? Can I even get close enough to knock him out? Hard to calculate when the ground keeps exploding.

A second squad of arena guards rushes the mage from the side, blades leveled at his back. The mage tracks their boots through the sand without turning, snapping a wide fan of fire that incinerates the reinforcements while keeping three geysers chasing my heels.

"Velgos, do your job!" the announcer shrieks from the balcony. "Kill him! Slay the elementalist before he burns the pavilion!"

Velgos snarls at the balcony, then turns a predatory gaze toward the mage, scimitars held low while keeping Leila in his peripheral vision. With the guards reduced to smoking grease, the mage wheels toward the approaching troll, raising two trembling hands to hold him at bay.

"Stay back!" the mage shrieks, voice fraying with panic. "I'll reduce you to cinders!"

"Try it," Velgos rumbles, his heavy boots crunching steadily over the scorched dirt.

The mage screams and releases a colossal column of flame, twice as wide as the earlier geysers, completely engulfing the troll in a roaring inferno. 

Velgos walks straight through the white-hot core without breaking stride. His anti-magic plating gleams pristine beneath the smoke, tusks bared in a cruel sneer.

"Die, beast!" The mage lunges forward in desperation, stabbing wildly at the troll's iron breastplate.

The dagger skitters uselessly off enchanted steel. The mage adjusts his grip to stab at the exposed neck, but Velgos bats the strike aside with his left scimitar and brings his right blade across in a devastating horizontal cleave, shearing the mage in two.

Before the body hits the sand, Leila darts into the troll's blind spot. Her enchanted dagger flashes across his exposed neck in one blinding stroke, and she brings her wooden sandal down to crush the severed head into bone meal.

}
#if(v_agility < 2) {
 

"You!" the mage howls, raising burning hands. "You set me up! I'll burn your flesh to the bone!"

"Hold on, let's talk about—"

A roaring lance of orange flame cuts me off, streaking across the sand at chest height.

I scramble backward to dodge the jet, but the moment my boots touch the sand, the ground detonates in a pillar of white-hot fire. The heat engulfs me instantly. My senses black out before the pain can even register, and my body reduces to ash in the dirt.

}
