#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0) {
 My dagger is enough. Extra steel only rattles and weighs down my footwork.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 1) {
 Extra reach is never a bad investment. I slide one of the scimitars into its leather sheath and buckle the strap to my belt.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 2) {
 Leaving enchanted steel in the dirt is throwing money away. I slide both scimitars into their scabbards and fix the dual baldric across my hips.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 1) {
 "Human," the lead ogre rumbles in his native tongue, leaning on his timber club. "The troll is dead. We have kept our word. Deliver the pen."

"Corridor closest to the gladiators' locker rooms," I reply in the same dialect. "Head through that iron gate, take the first left, and look for the heavy barred oak doors. Your clan is in the end cell."

"If this is a trick..."

"Leave him," the second ogre grunts, hauling his club. "He kept his word. Move before the garrison mobilizes."

The two massive brutes break into a heavy jog, thundering toward the inner service gate to stage their jailbreak.

Bruce stares after them, brow furrowed. "What just happened? What were you barking at them? Why are you letting the monsters walk?"

"The objective was to drop the troll," I say, wiping my blade. "Nobody said we had to execute the ogres."

"Why did they turn on Velgos in the first place?"

"Hostages," I say. "Velgos had their shaman and clan members locked in the sublevels to force them onto the sand. I gave them the room number in exchange for their clubs."

"You let them loose to get reinforcements?" Bruce's jaw drops.

"Reinforcements for what? They're going to grab their family and sprint for the city gates before the garrison forms ranks. If they smash a few arena handlers on the way out, that's Venard's problem. Don't bring mountain ogres into a civilian amphitheater if you don't want your guards crushed."

"Fine," Bruce grunts, shaking his head. "Forget the brutes. What now? Is the match called or what?"

"We wait for the voice in the box," I say. "He has to officially ring the bell."

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 2) {
 "So," Bruce says, kicking the sand off his boots. "Is the wave done, or are we standing around admiring the scenery?"

"We wait for the announcer," I say. "He has to officially call the end of the round."

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 0 && v_b2_ch5_strategy != 2 || v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 0 && v_b2_ch5_first_cut != 0 && v_b2_ch5_wilhelm != 0) {
 Bruce jogs over from the perimeter, wiping blood from his knuckles.

"You dropped the troll already?" he asks, eyes wide as he looks at the corpse.

"Finished him minutes ago," I say. "What kept you?"

"So... is the match over?" Bruce looks around the silent stands. "What are we standing around for?"

"We wait for the announcer," I say. "He has to officially call the end of the round."

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_first_cut == 0 && v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 0 && v_b2_ch5_strategy == 2 && v_b2_ch5_wilhelm != 0 || v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 0 && v_b2_ch5_strategy == 2 && v_b2_ch5_wilhelm == 0 && v_b2_ch2_cell != 1 || v_b2_ch5_negotiate == 0 && v_b2_ch5_strategy == 2 && v_b2_ch5_wilhelm == 0 && v_b2_ch5_first_cut != 0) {
 "Don't think I've forgotten what you pulled, you bastard!" the fire mage snarls, marching up with his fists clenched.

"Forgotten what?"

"You used me as bait!"

"Oh, that!" I wave a hand casually. "Tell you what. Next round, you use me as bait, and we'll call it even. Deal?"

"The next round is individual duels!" he yells.

"Is it?" I shrug. "Fine, the round after that, then."

"There is no round after that! It's just an optional exhibition match!"

"Technically it's only optional if you haven't broken the rules, but fair point," I say, tapping my chin. "Looks like we can't settle the score. Shame. No hard feelings though, right?"

}
