ID: B2-Ch05a-Smoothly
TEXT:

 The announcer finally re-emerges on the balcony, adjusting his collar with tight, nervous fingers.

"Pray accept our apologies for the delay, ladies and gentlemen," his voice rings out over the sand. "Following consultations with arena master Venard, we have determined that the second round cannot proceed following the demise of Velgos the mercenary. Consequently, the conclusion of this bout marks the end of the second wave. The third and final round will commence shortly, once the staging committee completes its preparations."

He leans over the brass railing, glaring down at our division.

"All gladiators will remain confined to their designated quarters until the final round begins. Roaming the service corridors is strictly prohibited. Your doors will remain bolted from the outside until match time. We will have no further... irregularities."

His glare fixes directly on my face. Still bitter about my early stroll onto the sand, apparently. Not that it matters; my notes on the remaining roster are already memorized.

Guards herd us back through the iron portcullis. The heavy oak door thuds shut behind us, and the iron bolt slides into place. 

Almost immediately, furious shouting carries through the wood from the hallway. The voice belongs to the ambassador of Ollendor.

"What do you mean, smoothly?" the ambassador shrieks. "Are you mocking me, Venard?"

"Not at all, Ambassador," Venard's smooth, cultured voice replies. "The tournament proceedings have followed established arena custom at every stage."

"Established custom? The killers of the Earl of Ollendor are still breathing, and you call that established custom?"

"I assure you," Venard says mildly, "our guests have received no special favors in the arena. Quite the contrary. If you harbor concerns regarding the matchups, you remain entirely free to consult the staging committee to adjust the final card. As always, the embassy maintains final authority over tournament scheduling."

"I was a fool to leave the matter in your hands!" the ambassador snarls. "If your handlers are too incompetent to arrange a proper execution, I shall handle the matchups myself!"

Heavy bootsteps storm down the passage, heading toward the staging offices.

"A pleasant afternoon to you as well, Ambassador," Venard calls after him, calm and unbothered, followed by the soft click of his boots departing.

Glowing blue letters float in the air in front of me. "It sounds like someone holds quite a grudge against you," Leila writes.

"Let him try," I say, leaning back against the cool stone wall. "He's running out of monsters."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch05b-Similar, v_current_scene = B2-Ch05b-Similar)
